    "background_story": "Jesus was a renowned chef in a small town in the French countryside. He was particularly famous for his signature dessert, a rich and flavorful fruit compote made with the freshest seasonal ingredients. Every summer, Jesus would spend hours in the local markets, carefully selecting the ripest strawberries, blueberries, and raspberries to create his masterpiece. His compote was a staple at family gatherings and special occasions, with people coming from all over to taste his delicious creation. Jesus's passion for cooking was inspired by his grandmother, who taught him the art of traditional French cuisine. He continued her legacy, experimenting with new flavors and ingredients while remaining true to his roots. Jesus's compote became a symbol of warmth, hospitality, and the joy of sharing meals with loved ones.",
